course: dictionary
lesson: 15390
title: Speedwell, a tiny blue wildflower
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A speedwell is a small wild plant. You will find it growing low down in grass, on lawns and in hedges, and nobody has to plant it there.
explain: Its flowers are tiny and bright blue. «Tiny speedwells dotted the lawn like specks of blue paint.» Dotted tells you they were spread here and there, and specks tells you how small they were.
explain: Speedwell is a noun, so it names a thing: the plant. Ask yourself, what is the thing here? It is a plant, not a bird or a path. Its plural is speedwells: «We found two speedwells in the hedge.»
fact: A speedwell is a small wild plant.
fact: Speedwell has tiny, bright blue flowers.
fact: «Speedwell» is a noun, and its plural is speedwells.
fact: In the UK and Ireland, speedwell is one of the easiest blue flowers to spot in spring.
fact: Its old name, bird's-eye, comes from the white centre of the flower.
exercise: «Tiny speedwells dotted the lawn.» What is a speedwell? | A large tree with red leaves | *A small wild plant with tiny bright blue flowers | A bird that sings in the hedge | A kind of stone found on hills
exercise: Where might you find speedwell growing? | Inside a sandcastle | In a classroom cupboard | At the bottom of the sea | *In grass, on lawns and in hedges
exercise: In the UK and Ireland, when is speedwell easiest to spot? | In winter, when it snows | Only at Christmas | *In spring | In the middle of the night
test: «We found two speedwells in the hedge.» Which word is the plural of speedwell? | speedwelling | speedwelled | speedwell | *speedwells
test: Why is speedwell sometimes called bird's-eye? | It can fly | It has a long beak | It has feathers | *It has a white centre
exam: Read: «Tiny speedwells dotted the lawn like specks of blue paint.» What does dotted most likely mean? | *Spread out here and there | Cut into long strips | Hidden under the snow | Stacked in a neat pile
